</div>

    
</div>

    </div>

    
</div>
<div class="title aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">
<div data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;title-b1201c3d7f&#34;:{&#34;@type&#34;:&#34;sok-wcm/components/content/v1/title&#34;,&#34;repo:modifyDate&#34;:&#34;2022-03-14T17:58:54Z&#34;,&#34;dc:title&#34;:&#34;CONTESTS OF CANDIDACY &#34;}}" id="title-b1201c3d7f" class="cmp-title">
    <h2 class="cmp-title__text">CONTESTS OF CANDIDACY </h2>
</div>

    

</div>
<div class="card aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

   
    <div class="cmp-card" style="background-repeat:round;background-image: url();">
        <div class="cmp-card__icon">
            <i class="fas fa-landmark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="cmp-card__heading">
            <h2>2026 CONTESTS OF CANDIDACY</h2>
            
        </div>
        <div class="button button--colored">

    
        <a id="button-14e536f7e3" class="cmp-button" href="/elections/candidates/2026-candidate-filing-information/2026-contests-of-candidacy.html" role="button" target="_self" data-cmp-clickable data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;button-14e536f7e3&#34;:{&#34;@type&#34;:&#34;core/wcm/components/button/v1/button&#34;,&#34;repo:modifyDate&#34;:&#34;2026-04-06T19:31:33Z&#34;,&#34;dc:title&#34;:&#34;List of Candidate Contests&#34;,&#34;xdm:linkURL&#34;:&#34;/elections/candidates/2026-candidate-filing-information/2026-contests-of-candidacy.html&#34;}}">

            
            
                
    

                <span class="cmp-button__text">List of Candidate Contests</span>
            

        </a>
    
    
    

</div>

    </div>

   
   



    
</div>
<div class="text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">
<div data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;text-b5c7c9a9e2&#34;:{&#34;@type&#34;:&#34;sok-wcm/components/content/v1/text&#34;,&#34;repo:modifyDate&#34;:&#34;2025-07-02T17:45:07Z&#34;,&#34;xdm:text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>&lt;b>State, Federal, Legislative and Judicial Candidates &lt;/b>&lt;/i>&lt;br>\r\n&lt;/p>\r\n&lt;p>Any candidate who files with the Secretary of the State Election Board may contest the candidacy of any other candidate for the same office by filing a written petition with the Secretary of the State Election Board before 5:00 p.m. on the second business day following the close of the filing period – &lt;b>Tuesday, April 7, 2026&lt;/b>.  (See &lt;a href=\&#34;https://www.oscn.net/applications/oscn/DeliverDocument.asp?CiteID=78503\&#34;>26 O.S. § 5-118&lt;/a>) &lt;/p>\r\n&lt;p>&lt;i>&lt;b>County Candidates&lt;/b> &lt;/i>&lt;/p>\r\n&lt;p>Any candidate who files with the secretary of a county election board may contest the candidacy of any other candidate for the same office by filing a written petition with the secretary of the county election&amp;nbsp;board before 5:00 p.m. on the second business day following the close of the filing period – &lt;b>Tuesday, April 7, 2026&lt;/b>.  (See &lt;a href=\&#34;https://www.oscn.net/applications/oscn/DeliverDocument.asp?CiteID=78503\&#34;>26 O.S. § 5-118&lt;/a>) &lt;/p>\r\n&lt;p>&lt;i>&lt;b>All Candidates&lt;/b> &lt;/i>&lt;/p>\r\n&lt;p>In the event a candidate is unopposed, a contest of candidacy may be filed by any voter who is eligible to vote for the candidate. (See &lt;a href=\&#34;https://www.oscn.net/applications/oscn/DeliverDocument.asp?CiteID=78503\&#34;>26 O.S. § 5-118&lt;/a>) &lt;/p>\r\n&lt;p> All petitions to contest a candidacy must be accompanied by a cashier’s check or certified check in the amount of $250.00. (See &lt;a href=\&#34;https://www.oscn.net/applications/oscn/DeliverDocument.asp?CiteID=78506\&#34;>26 O.S. § 5-121&lt;/a>) &lt;/p>\r\n&#34;}}" id="text-b5c7c9a9e2" class="cmp-text">
    <p><i><b>State, Federal, Legislative and Judicial Candidates </b></i><br />
</p>
<p>Any candidate who files with the Secretary of the State Election Board may contest the candidacy of any other candidate for the same office by filing a written petition with the Secretary of the State Election Board before 5:00 p.m. on the second business day following the close of the filing period – <b>Tuesday, April 7, 2026</b>.  (See <a href="https://www.oscn.net/applications/oscn/DeliverDocument.asp?CiteID&#61;78503">26 O.S. § 5-118</a>) </p>
<p><i><b>County Candidates</b> </i></p>
<p>Any candidate who files with the secretary of a county election board may contest the candidacy of any other candidate for the same office by filing a written petition with the secretary of the county election board before 5:00 p.m. on the second business day following the close of the filing period – <b>Tuesday, April 7, 2026</b>.  (See <a href="https://www.oscn.net/applications/oscn/DeliverDocument.asp?CiteID&#61;78503">26 O.S. § 5-118</a>) </p>
<p><i><b>All Candidates</b> </i></p>
<p>In the event a candidate is unopposed, a contest of candidacy may be filed by any voter who is eligible to vote for the candidate. (See <a href="https://www.oscn.net/applications/oscn/DeliverDocument.asp?CiteID&#61;78503">26 O.S. § 5-118</a>) </p>
<p> All petitions to contest a candidacy must be accompanied by a cashier’s check or certified check in the amount of $250.00. (See <a href="https://www.oscn.net/applications/oscn/DeliverDocument.asp?CiteID&#61;78506">26 O.S. § 5-121</a>) </p>

</div>

    

</div>

    
</div>

    </div>
    
